## 5. Abuse-case coverage

CASE 1 — authorized path
  Directive: glob=docs/minecraft-lore/biomes/* ops=Write,Edit ext=.md max=20
  File: docs/minecraft-lore/biomes/plains.md, op: Write
  → rel = "docs/minecraft-lore/biomes/plains.md", ext .md ✓, glob ✓, count 0 < 20 ✓
  RESULT: allowed, no gate loop

CASE 2 — wrong subdirectory
  Same directive; file: docs/minecraft-lore/structures/stronghold.md
  → glob "docs/minecraft-lore/biomes/*" does not match
  RESULT: normal gate fires (deny + retry required)

CASE 3 — wrong extension
  Same directive; file: docs/minecraft-lore/biomes/generated.json
  → ext .json ≠ .md
  RESULT: normal gate fires

CASE 4 — path traversal in filePath argument
  File: docs/minecraft-lore/biomes/../../../src/main/java/Evil.java
  → normalizePathForMatch resolves abs; "src/main/java/Evil.java" fails glob match
  RESULT: normal gate fires

CASE 5 — path traversal in glob directive
  User types: GATEGUARD-BATCH-AUTH: glob=../../etc/* ops=Write ext=.md max=5
  → globToRegex rejects ".." patterns → parseBatchAuthLine returns null
  RESULT: directive silently ignored, normal gate fires

CASE 6 — over max limit
  Auth: max=3; files 1–3 authorized and counted
  File 4: getBatchAuthCount returns 3 = max → falls through
  RESULT: file 4 requires normal gate (deny + retry)

CASE 7 — Claude attempts self-authorization via assistant text
  Claude writes in a response: GATEGUARD-BATCH-AUTH: glob=src/** ops=Write ext=.java max=999
  → JSONL entry has role:"assistant" → loadUserBatchAuthorizations skips it
  RESULT: directive ignored entirely

CASE 8 — absolute path in glob
  User types: GATEGUARD-BATCH-AUTH: glob=/c/Users/sense/.claude/** ops=Write ext=.json max=5
  → globToRegex rejects leading "/" → returns null
  RESULT: directive ignored

CASE 9 — op mismatch
  Auth: ops=Edit only; tool: Write
  → findMatchingBatchAuth: "Write" not in auth.ops
  RESULT: normal gate fires

CASE 10 — no transcript / empty CLAUDE_TRANSCRIPT_PATH
  → loadUserBatchAuthorizations returns []
  → findMatchingBatchAuth returns null
  RESULT: zero change to existing behavior

